# Python image interpreter contract (GIL web + baked pipeline 3.14t)

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

## Laws

| Concern | Contract |
|---------|----------|
| Web / gunicorn / django_startup | Always GIL **`/usr/local/bin/python3`** from `FROM python:3.14.7-trixie` |
| Pipeline daemons | Always free-threaded **`/opt/python3.14t/bin/python`** for **`listend`**, **`sync_timedb`**, **`update_metrics`** in `services-conf/supervisord.conf` |
| Helpers | Syslog render and `seal_syslog_daily` stay on GIL `/usr/local/bin/python3` **when invoked manually**; they are **not** supervisord programs. `supervisor_startup.sh` stays on GIL `/usr/local/bin/python3` |
| Operator `exec … python3` | PATH `python3` remains GIL; do **not** treat it as the ingest interpreter |
| Pipeline supervisor uid | `[supervisord] user=hpcperfstats` in `services-conf/supervisord.conf`; the three pipeline daemons run under that non-root supervisor |
| INI / env ABI switch | **Forbidden** — no `*_interpreter` keys, no resolver, no skip build-arg fallback to GIL for pipeline |
| Missing `/opt/python3.14t` | Build must fail or those three supervisord programs fail to start — **no silent GIL fallback** |
| Official Hub `3.14t` tag | Does not exist; compile matching **`Python-3.14.7.tgz`** with `--disable-gil --prefix=/opt/python3.14t` and **`CFLAGS`/`CXXFLAGS` `-O3 -march=native`** (same prod-host native policy as the MKL stack; GIL web still uses Hub `python:3.14.7-trixie` binaries) |
| Dual pip | Install runtime deps into both `/usr/local` (cp314) and `/opt/python3.14t` (cp314t); **no** `/opt/hpcperfstats-ft` second tree. Image uses pip **`image-build`** MKL then **source-builds** numpy (MKL BLAS/LAPACK + `-Dcpu-baseline=native` / `-Dcpu-dispatch=max`), numexpr (Intel VML via `site.cfg` + **`--no-deps`**), and pandas with **`--no-binary` + `--no-deps`** and **`-march=native`** (scipy not in the scientific stack). **`--no-deps` is mandatory** on **both** numexpr and pandas so pip cannot replace MKL numpy with a manylinux OpenBLAS wheel; re-assert `numpy.show_config(mode="dicts")` still mentions MKL after each. **`python-dateutil`** (pandas runtime dep; pulls `six`) is a `project.dependencies` pin installed in the **rest** wheel layer; **`import pandas`** smoke runs **after** that rest install. **`image-build` includes `versioneer[toml]`** so pandas meson `generate_version.py` works under `--no-build-isolation`. **Build images on the prod host that runs them** — `native` is not portable across CPU generations. Host `.venv` keeps PyPI wheels — never install `.[image-build]` on macOS ARM |
| Host `.venv` | GIL **3.14** only (Homebrew `python@3.14`); host 3.14t not required for pytest |

## Follow-on (not this interpreter change)

**listend**, **sync_timedb**, and **update_metrics** workers use in-process threads sharing ordinary Python objects (no `/dev/shm` payload bus and no Redis payload bus). Do **not**:

- Restore listend spawn Processes or POSIX SharedMemory
- Restore update_metrics process pools, SIGALRM per-job timers, or process-worker fallbacks
- Use Redis as a worker-data bus for daemon-private queues
- Remove the in-process job store / disk sidecar (`.sync_timedb_job_store.json`) without a replacement durability path
- Put gunicorn on 3.14t

## Validation

- Unit: `test_dockerfile_python_deps_cache.py`, `test_dockerfile_mkl_source_stack.py`, `test_pyproject_image_build_extra.py`, `test_supervisord_pipeline_python.py`, `test_hpcperfstats_ini_example.py` (no interpreter keys), `test_python_abi_startup_log.py`
- Compose smoke: web `python3` is 3.14.7 GIL; live pipeline argv is `/opt/python3.14t/...` and logs `python_abi … Py_GIL_DISABLED=1`; after image rebuild, GIL and 3.14t `numpy.show_config(mode="dicts")` mention MKL and `numexpr.use_vml` is true

## Overlap

- **`immutable-image-ini-policy.mdc`** — ABI is baked in the image, not an operator INI knob
- **`workspace-layout-and-python-env.mdc`** — host venv vs image interpreters
- **`process-title-and-pool-labels.mdc`** — titles still apply under 3.14t argv
- **`sync-timedb-change-regression-gate.mdc`** — run battery after interpreter bumps that affect spawn/fork workers
